  "$comment": "Candlelight's cooking pan. The station hides the block wherever this scene is drawn, with somebody at it or not, and shows it here (the pan tells the clients what lies in it): the same pan, x and z 3..13, walls 1 px up to the rim at y 4 round a floor y 0..1 (inside x and z 4..12, floor y 1), one long handle out of the block on its west side, x -5..3, y 1..3, as the block faces north; no lid, as the block has none. The scene faces the cook; the code turns the pan to the way the block stands. It is the roaster's scene without a lid: six places for what roasts, as the pan's own six slots, lying on its floor; the pan is taken by its handle and swirled as a soup is stirred; the roast that is done lies in the pan, not in a slot: a bowl takes a serving. Over a campfire it stands on Farm & Charm's grate. The camera looks down more steeply than at the roaster (58 degrees against 49), from further back, at a point nearer the cook and lower: the pan is shallow, and at the roaster's angle its front wall hid what had slid against it; its handle, 8 px out of the pan whichever way the block stands, stays in the frame, over the inventory row when it points at the cook. The camera aims 2 px to the cook's left of the pan's middle, so the pan stands a little right of the screen's middle and a handle pointing left reaches under the open book with its tip only. The book opens where it opens at every station, so the cook finds it in the same place; the badge stands higher than at the roaster, so that a handle pointing right passes under it.",
